'''Concordia Rapid Transit''' ({{Lang-bl|Tránsito Rápido Concordia}}; '''CRT'''), originally the '''Alpujarra Rapid Transit''' ('''ART''') is a multimodal amalgamation of {{W|heavy rail}} {{W|elevated railway|elevated}} and {{W|Rapid transit|subway}} {{W|public transportation}} systems serving the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]] within [[Balisca]]. CRT serves [[List of Concordia Rapid Transit stations|623 stations]] along 36 routes on {{convert|1587.3|km|sp=us}} of {{W|rapid transit}} lines. If considered a single unified system, the CRT is the [[List of metro systems in Adonia|busiest heavy rail rapid transit system in Adonia]].

The initial system within the CRT opened in stages from 1909 to 1912 within the [[Ampurias]] and [[Expansión]] boroughs as the "Castejón Underground". It is operated by the [[Concordia Rapid Transit Authority]] which formed in 2019 following the voluntary association of the respective transit authorities via interregional compact. The system was extended most recently in June 2021, when [[Civitas station|Civitas]] and [[North Del Mar station|North Del Mar]] stations opened as part of the [[Concordia Rapid Transit extension II]] under the administration of the [[Jatiel Transportation Authority|Jatiel Transportation Corporation]] (JTC).



